rm memory for objects</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2006</year><volume>440</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16382240</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nature04262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenlee</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Magnussen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Reinvang</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Brain regions involved in spatial frequency discrimination: evidence from fMRI</article-title><source>Exp Brain Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>132</volume><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>403</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10883389</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s002210000385</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fuster</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>prefrontal cortex &#x02013; an update: time is of the essence</article-title><source>Neuron</source><year>2001</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>333</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11394996</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0896-6273(01)00285-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldman-Rakic</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Architecture of the prefrontal cortex and the central executive</article-title><source>Ann N Y Acad Sci</source><year>1995</year><volume>769</volume><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8595045</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1749-6632.1995.tb38132.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-n